WEBVTT

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.200
Who wants some mandarin orange?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.700
Where are we right now?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.950
Stop leaning forward.
Don't blame me if you get sick.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.950
I don't get carsick!

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.580
Seriously? We only have 30 minutes to bathe?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.620
But I like taking long baths!

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.410
The time schedule isn't set in stone...

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.950
Who wants candy?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.250
We're totally in the mountains now, huh?

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.080
It feels like we're in a resort town.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.370
Hmph. It's just a regular countryside.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.870
Just to be clear, I didn't
come because I wanted to.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.620
You can't push that!

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.660
Stopping at the next stop.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.410
Sorry, we're not getting off!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.950
That's not the button to call the tour guide?

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.910
Normal buses don't have them.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:20.120
Going back in time to when we, Team Otori,
had just finished our first performance,

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.540
the Newcomers' Debut Performance--

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:29.620
The Ayanagi Festival in October.
The performance there will be the next test stage.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.200
Ayanagi Festival...?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.200
Is there a piece we have to perform?

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.580
Unlike the debut performance, each group
is free to decide what they want to perform.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.790
Does that mean we can decide ourselves?

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.830
That's kind of exciting.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.830
It's not as easy as you think.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.290
That's right.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:51.500
And so, during the upcoming summer vacation,
Team Otori will have a training camp.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.040
Training camp?!

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.500
You amateurs can go to a
training camp by yourselves.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.160
I'll stay home with Tavian--

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.950
It'd be lonely without you, Tengenji!

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.450
I wouldn't feel lonely.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.450
What?!

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:09.200
By the way, Tengenji, you seem to be
reading the guide rather enthusiastically.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.160
What?!

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.330
Because Nayuki said
he stayed up working on it...

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.830
Could they actually be a good combination?

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.200
Maybe.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.500
Otori, sir, our training camp will be
at the Hiragi family villa, right?

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.620
You can expect a lot.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.370
It's the famous Hiragi
family's mansion, after all.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.410
It <i>is</i> a mansion...

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.370
...but it's really run-down.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.290
Now, boys. Hurry up and come in.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:52.410
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:59.790
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:06.910
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:14.750
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.250
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:22.790
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:31.040
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:37.290
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.330
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:45.830
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.540
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:55.290
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.580
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.950
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:04.500
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:12.000
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.000
"Act 7"

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.290
The first floor is the hall and practice room,

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.540
and the second floor is the accommodations.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.580
You can use whatever room you'd like.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:25.950
That looks expensive!

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.450
Hey, don't touch it and break it--

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.200
What's with this floor?!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.450
Why is it so run-down?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:37.830
Hm, it looks like no one's used it for a while.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.580
Well, it won't keep us from practicing.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.410
Sir, where is the practice room?

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.000
Forget that.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.290
We're all tired from traveling since morning.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:55.700
Making sure your body gets enough
rest is also part of an actor's training.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:59.660
Well, have fun, boys!

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.410
Even if he tells us, "have fun"...

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:06.910
What are we supposed to do
this deep in the mountains?!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.250
We've gotta start with exploring!

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.200
Wait, Hoshitani!

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.660
Wh-What?

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.370
"Beware of Bears"

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.540
Bears...?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.830
It'd be all right if it was a cub...

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.830
Cubs are scary, too!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.540
Hoshitani, are you bad with animals in general?

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.290
Wh-Wh-What was that just now?

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:34.580
Did you hear something from in there?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.540
That's the food storage shed, right?

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.450
What was that scream?

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.080
Nayuki!

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.410
What happened?

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.250
Th-Th-There's a bear!

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.040
What?!

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.250
Where is it?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.660
In here!

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.750
What's that?

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:15.700
I threw it by accident... I wonder if it hurt?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.040
Let's all hold the door together!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.450
R-Right!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.120
Oh, that scared me.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.790
I've got a bump now...

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.950
I was just getting some food...

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.830
Oh, I know you! You guys are from Team Otori!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.410
And I believe you're...

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.200
I am...

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:01.250
That's right! I'm Ayanagi Academy's
singing and dancing new star!

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:04.700
From Team Hiragi, Seishiro Inumine!

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:07.580
That's me!

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.080
"Beware of Bears"

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:26.000
♪ We are the dazzling Top of Star ♪

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.410
♪ Our team is number one! ♪

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:33.160
♪ We received the gift of talent ♪

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:37.330
♪ We were born stars of stars ♪

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:40.870
♪ There are no mistakes in our fan service ♪

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:44.200
♪ We'll give you a sparkling wink! ♪

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:47.580
♪ Without a single misstep ♪

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.410
♪ We're perfectly synced ♪

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:54.750
♪ Let's Dance! Sing a Song! ♪

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:59.080
♪ We're dashing up to stardom right now ♪

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.500
♪ The promised main stage ♪

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.910
♪ With precise steps ♪

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.250
♪ We bring along our aspirations ♪

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:13.580
♪ There are no rivals here ♪

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:16.950
♪ Five perfect personalities ♪

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:21.870
♪ We're proud of what only we can do ♪

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:30.450
♪ Look, we'll show you a perfect performance ♪

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.410
Team Hiragi?!

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:47.500
Hey, when did you guys wander off?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.750
The next thing I knew,
no one else was around, and that--

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.620
That's <i>our</i> line, Inu, you dog!

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.040
We were looking everywhere for you.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:59.250
He's useless for anything except musicals.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.450
Well? Why is Team Otori here?

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.160
Waited long enough to ask.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.580
We're probably here for
the same reason you guys are.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.160
Huh? Am I still dreaming?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.410
I didn't expect you to also use this place.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:29.120
At any rate, I can't believe you
could sleep in such a dusty room.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.160
I wonder about your senses.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:34.040
You're really sensitive, huh?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.120
You are not sensitive enough.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.620
Excuse us!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.330
Please excuse us.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:43.830
Oh my. This is kind of a refreshing sight.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:48.330
Hiragi, sir, we have
successfully recovered Inumine.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.660
Good work.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:55.410
Otori, sir, did you know that Team Hiragi
would be having their training camp here?

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.660
We got here first.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.160
You guys should leave!

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.450
What? <i>You</i> guys should leave!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.870
What did you say?!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.950
What shall we do, Hiragi, sir?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:12.040
It's fine for everyone to stay, don't you think?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.660
No road is long with good company.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:18.790
Take this opportunity to get
to know each other, boys.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.540
Thanks for the food!

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.250
Thanks for making our lunch, too.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:36.370
I hope you liked it.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:38.660
I can eat anything other than rocks.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.450
That's not a compliment.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.330
Team Hiragi has practice
this afternoon, too, huh?

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:48.500
Why do those boors have
practice while we have to clean?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.910
It's fine! We don't have practice today.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.500
Besides, all that's left is the
master bedroom on the second floor.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.620
Woah, it's completely different from our rooms.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.160
The master bedroom, huh?

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.290
I'm sure Otori or Hiragi will use it.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:09.000
Oh, look! There's that famous
frilly thing on top of the bed!

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.200
You're right! I've never seen one before!

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.620
Hey, look...

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:14.620
What?

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.080
Is that Otori and Hiragi?

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.120
Oh, they look close!

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.660
Because they're related.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.160
Really?

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.540
The Otori family is a
branch of the Hiragi family.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.410
We're done! We're done!

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:35.750
In the end, we spent all day cleaning, huh?

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:39.830
What's that sound?

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.950
Probably a mouse or something.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.290
What, Hoshitani?
Mice are only this big, you know.

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:47.370
Oh, Team Otori!

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.950
You were really cleaning until now.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.620
Thanks for your hard work.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.750
We weren't doing it for <i>you</i> !

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.160
Ugawa, thank them properly.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:57.620
T-Tatsumin...

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:03.500
Hah, I guess you're scared
of Mommy, huh? Little Ugawa.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.540
What the hell? You guys
are the ones playing house.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.040
You're just a motley bunch!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.200
What'd you say?!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:09.910
Motley bunch!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:10.700
Ugawa!

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.910
Tengenji!

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.910
We're not a motley bunch!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:12.870
Motley bunch!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.450
Oh no, that vase is expensive!

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.620
I'll get it out of the way!

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.700
I'll help, too!

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.500
Be careful!

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.750
I can't believe it ended
in such a clichéd way...

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.410
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should we do?!

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:42.450
How much is this?!

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:45.200
It's a famous German brand, huh?

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.200
It can't be less than a hundred million.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.410
A hundred million?!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:52.160
That vase was Chekhov's gun, huh?

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:57.410
He means, there are no
unnecessary props on stage.

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:59.620
What was that sound just now?

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.370
Anyway, just hide it!

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:03.120
Everything okay?

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:08.660
Why are you dressed like that?

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:14.830
Oh, who took off their clothes
and left them here?

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:20.160
Oh dear.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.330
What is the meaning of this?

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.370
W-Well...

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.250
W-We...

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.700
"Scene of carnage at the Hiragi family villa
--Mental image"

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.330
A-A bear did it!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.950
What?!

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:36.620
Wait, a bear?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.500
Isn't that pushing it?

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:42.000
I wanted to protect Hoshitani and
Inumine and couldn't help myself...

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.620
Thanks.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.080
There's no helping what was already said.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:46.870
Let's see this through.

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.040
Put on an act, huh?

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.120
Well, where's the bear?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:54.250
U-Um, over there!

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:57.000
That's right, over there!

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:02.000
I-It looked like it was in a hurry
and left right away. Um...

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.160
Through the window.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.660
It's closed!

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:09.410
H-How conscientious of him
to close it after he opened it.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.250
There's no way a bear like that exists.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.700
What's your deal?!

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.790
Calm down, everyone!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.580
♪ Do not be afraid ♪

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.120
♪ Everything's fine ♪

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:26.870
♪ I think Mr. Bear already
went back home to the woods ♪

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:28.200
What is he doing?

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.700
Everyone, let's all say "bye" to Mr. Bear!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.700
Don't worry.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.200
That's normal for Inumine. See?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.200
Mr. Bear, bye-bye!

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:36.660
Hiragi doesn't look like he suspects anything.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:36.660
Come on, all together now!

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.830
Bye-by--

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.830
That's enough.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.250
Anyway, it's dangerous,
so clean up the fragments.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.250
Wait a minute!

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.040
It'd be better not to touch it.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:50.080
Hiragi, wouldn't it be
better to purify it first?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.950
Wait, what do you mean "purify"?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:57.160
This is an unlucky vase that has been passed
down in the Hiragi family for generations.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.700
Unlucky vase?

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:02.620
All who touched this vase in
the past died, one after another.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:05.250
Apparently, there were talks to dispose of it,

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.620
but it is a vase that
invites death with a touch.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.750
No one knew what to do with it.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:13.660
Th-That's a lie...

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.750
Right, Hiragi, sir?

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:21.040
I'm glad it was a bear that broke it...

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.910
Before it was broken by a person,
however unlikely that is.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:30.620
Um, if it <i>was</i> a person who broke it,
what would happen to him?

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:33.500
I'm afraid to even imagine...

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:39.450
It's possible that something
worse than death awaits...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.830
Look! What's that?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:03.620
It seemed funny,
so I couldn't help but go along with it.

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:09.250
Of course, we knew from the beginning
that you were the ones who broke the vase.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:12.120
I-I'm so sorry!

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:13.790
The others had nothing to do with it.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.540
So the two of us will pay for it...

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:17.700
But in installments, if possible...!

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:22.040
Don't be so hasty.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.330
This is a cheap replica.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.580
What?!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:28.790
You should have just told the truth.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:30.660
What...?

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:34.330
I had fun watching the
dream team perform together.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:38.080
Now, please get dinner ready.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.830
Oh, good...

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.500
I'm so glad!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:45.620
There was no way I'd be
able to pay a hundred million...

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.620
It looks like they believed us.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:49.160
A piece from an old and
distinguished German brand, was it?

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:53.200
Too bad. Looks like we've
lost a Hiragi family heirloom.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:56.580
I'll apologize to Grandfather.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.080
Thanks.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:03.540
Even so, I can't believe they
tried to trick us with their acting.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.910
Give it another ten years, boys.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.250
Practicing on your own?

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:11.290
Oh, it just seems strange
to skip a day of practice.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.870
You like musicals, don't you?

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:16.040
You do too, don't you, Tatsumi?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.660
I could tell watching you
at the debut performance.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.000
Your team's "Ayanagi Showtime"
wasn't bad, either.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.330
You think so?

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.950
But you're no threat to us.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.120
Maybe?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:32.250
That's my fault, isn't it?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:38.410
Out of curiosity, why are you
trying to be a musical actor?

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:41.080
Um, well, it's not about the musicals...

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:44.750
I just have someone I admire.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:48.540
But I only saw him once,
so I don't even know his name.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:55.910
I see. So musicals to you are
that person you admire, huh?

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:58.910
You don't know most of the famous works,

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:01.750
or many playwrights or directors.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.120
That's why you're pure and interesting.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:08.660
But you'll reach a limit one day with just that.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:09.910
Maybe.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:11.660
A limit?

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:15.330
The one who pulls the team and
helps them survive until the next stage...

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:19.040
The one who should make
decisions at important times...

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.040
That's you, the leader, isn't it?

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:26.910
At times like that, does the person
you admire give you advice?

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.120
That person is my dream...

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:36.200
No matter how clumsy I am,
no matter how little I know about musicals...

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:40.700
I don't know a way to give up on my dream.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.080
You are wonderful.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:46.700
Just like your team's performance.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.450
Your skill levels are all different,

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:51.080
and your performance looked like
it was put together last minute.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:55.330
But something about you shines.

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:58.080
I can't deny that I felt that.

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:59.160
Tatsumi...

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:00.910
Tatsumin!

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:04.250
Inumine looks like he's about to fall asleep!

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:07.080
I have to go.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.330
Thanks.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:09.870
Today was fun.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:13.040
I'm glad we could act together. Next time--

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.200
Hoshitani.

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:17.910
Today, we just happened to be on the same stage,

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.750
and became costars by a strange twist of fate.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.290
But don't forget--

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:28.040
Tomorrow, we'll go back to
being rivals fighting for the top spot.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:32.700
I'm looking forward to seeing
your team become formidable rivals.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.250
Yeah!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:47.830
Please put that away
<i>before</i> the underclassmen see it.

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.500
You really are too sensitive.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.450
You are not sensitive enough.

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:56.290
You won't notice the enemy
until you're stabbed in the back.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:58.160
That's a scary thing to say.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.790
I'm being serious.

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:04.700
Is that a warning from
the head of the Kao Council?

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.910
Or is that advice from a friend?

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:13.290
You never pay heed to
my advice. Like that time...

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.830
I'll call the police.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:21.290
Wait.

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:22.410
Look.

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.120
Hoshitani?

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:50.950
What's wrong, Hoshitani?

00:21:56.950 --> 00:22:00.040
I really want to sing right now!

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:04.040
What the heck?

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.290
I just want to sing!

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:22.160
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:32.200
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:36.500
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:40.620
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:43.870
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:47.450
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:22:47.450 --> 00:22:51.410
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:54.580
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:58.450
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:01.950
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:05.700
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:09.290
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:12.950
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:18.950
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:33.080
We're back!

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:35.830
Training camp is over,
and it's almost the end of vacation.

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:38.080
I hate to think about it.

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:40.950
But we did our homework
during the training camp,

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:43.000
so we can play starting from tomorrow, right?

00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:48.620
Why didn't you do your homework?

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:52.080
Hoshitani, once you finish that, do this.

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:26.700
"Act 8"

00:23:57.660 --> 00:24:00.580
Toraishi, Inumine already fell asleep,
so let me sleep in your room.

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:03.910
Aw, how cute. Did you watch
a scary TV show or something?

00:24:03.910 --> 00:24:07.200
That's not it. When that guy sleeps,
he grinds his teeth, eats rice balls,

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:09.370
and opens his eyes. Anyway, it's hard to relax!

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:11.330
Man, that guy really is useless...

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:26.700
"Look forward to next week, too.
Right, Inumine?"
